WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.960
A Japan Association of Music Enterprises
50th Anniversary Project

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.880
<i>"But what is it that will make</i>
<i>people happy?" continued Giovanni.</i>

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.840
<i>"I don't know,"</i>
<i>Campanella muttered.</i>

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:18.010
<i>"Anyway, we're going to hold on!" said</i>
<i>Giovanni with an explosion of breath</i>

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.470
<i>as if his chest were brimming</i>
<i>with new-found energy.</i>

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.940
from Kenji Miyazawa's
<i>"Night on the Galactic Railroad"</i>

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.820
<i>How many years</i>
<i>have passed since then?</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.910
<i>That was the year</i>
<i>we travelled to Shikotan,</i>

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.200
<i>the island where</i>
<i>we once lived.</i>

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.460
<i>To our old home,</i>
<i>full of so many memories.</i>

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.040
<i>To our lost island.</i>

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.030
Miss Sawako, we're almost
at the island.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.950
So we are.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:18.250
We've finally come back.
What's it been, 50 years?

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.880
It brings back a lot
of memories, doesn't it?

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.920
Not for me.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.720
I get rid of things I don't want
to remember with an eraser.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.100
Can you, though?

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.470
I suppose not.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.770
You can't get rid of them.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.900
I can't forget,
even if I want to.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.730
I'm sure it's the same
for you, Junpei.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.030
I suppose it is.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:56.370
<i>Our old home. The island</i>
<i>where stars fall to Earth.</i>

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:03.540
<i>The island of the Galactic Railroad.</i>
<i>Giovanni and Campanella's island.</i>

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:11.380
-<i>July, 1945...</i>
- July, 1945.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.760
Eggs, eggs, eggs, eggs...

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.230
Over here! Look at me!
Look at me!

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.310
No one's home!

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.280
- You can have the floaters, Kanta!
- No fair, Brother!

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.880
Got 'em.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.170
The floaters are the ones
that are about to hatch!

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.220
Here's your eggs back!

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.650
Sorry to bother you...

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.950
July 4, 1945

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:20.040
- Hey, wait!
- Hurry!

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.370
- Good afternoon, ladies!
- Hi, Junpei!

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.340
- Delivery, ma'am!
- It's so big! Look!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.300
- Delivery, ma'am!
- Thank you, Kanta.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.340
Have a good day, everyone!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.560
- Hello!
- Hello!

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.980
- Hey, boys!
- I wish I had their energy!

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.110
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.780
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.740
- We're home!
- We're home!

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.950
- Oh, there you are.
- That smells so good!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.200
- I'll cook you up some.
- I'll help!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.370
Good boy.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.080
Galactic Railroad, now departing!

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.630
All board who's coming aboard!

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.710
Hurry, we're now departing!

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.710
Depart station!

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.570
Campanella, hop on!
Hurry!

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.700
Wait for me, Giovanni!

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.120
Next stop is Cygnus Station!

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.040
Cygnus Station!

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:02.510
GIOVANNI'S ISLAND

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.770
Air raid alert!
This is an air raid alert!

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:11.650
More than 100 dive bombers
are advancing towards Nemuro!

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.730
Make for the air raid
shelter immediately!

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.490
Air raid alert!
This is an air raid alert!

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:29.250
I wonder if the Dawn Corps boys up in
the mountains will shoot them down?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.420
Darn it all.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.340
I think they're up too high
for their guns to reach.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:38.970
- Let's go to the shelter.
- Hurry.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.020
- Dad!
- Dad!

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.520
- Hurry and get to the shelter.
- Yes, sir.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.820
Father, look after the boys.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.150
Don't worry, son.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.620
<i>My father was the commander</i>
<i>of the island's defense force.</i>

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:10.830
<i>Well, in fact the real soldiers,</i>
<i>called the Dawn Corps,</i>

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.120
<i>are holed up</i>
<i>in the mountains.</i>

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.970
<i>He was basically the head of</i>
<i>the village's fire brigade.</i>

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.470
The war's finally come
all the way up here...

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.350
Nemuro is burning...

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:43.590
However, it is according to the
dictates of time and fate that

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:47.250
We have resolved to pave the
way for a grand peace

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.740
August 15, 1945

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.090
for all the generations to come

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:54.560
by enduring the unendurable
and suffering what is insufferable.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:07:00.480
Cultivate the ways of rectitude,
foster nobility of spirit

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:05.510
and keep pace with
the progress of the world

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:14.440
- What did His Majesty say?
- I couldn't hear very well...

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:19.230
- It's over...
- The war is over.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.740
<i>August 15th.</i>

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:29.700
<i>Japan... was defeated.</i>

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.330
Dad...

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.550
Don't worry.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.210
Even if the war is lost, as long
as we have our island...

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:45.220
As long as our people are still alive,
the country will never fall.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.230
What's going to happen
to the country now?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.810
The Americans will come
and make everybody into slaves.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.110
What?

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:03.110
Those Yanks are
red devils, after all.

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.360
You're joking...

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:08.410
There's no telling what they'll do
to you womenfolk if you don't hide.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.660
You better paint your faces black
to look like men.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.660
Stop trying to scare me!

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.910
Well, I'm off.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.880
Even if we've lost the war,
a fisherman has to fish.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.360
I'll have Kanta
do it today.

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.690
Kanta, will you
read this for us?

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.980
Yes, sir.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:53.040
"'What on earth can I do
for their happiness?'

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.540
Giovanni, completely despondent,
hung his head.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.050
'Who's to say it wasn't for the best?
However painful a thing might be...'"

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.340
<i>Our father loved Kenji Miyazawa's</i>
<i>"Night on the Galactic Railroad".</i>

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.760
<i>After I started primary school,</i>

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.350
<i>he had me read it out loud</i>
<i>almost every day, too.</i>

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:19.230
<i>He said that our mother loved</i>
<i>this book when she was alive.</i>

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:22.860
<i>We were named after</i>
<i>the characters, too.</i>

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:29.990
<i>Junpei comes from "Giovanni,"</i>
<i>and Kanta from "Campanella."</i>

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:40.080
September 1, 1945

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:45.670
- Miss Sawako, good morning!
- Good morning!

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.380
Good morning, Junpei, Kanta.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.890
Ma'am, do you think the
Americans will come?

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:55.720
Our grandpa said that the women
should run and hide!

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.930
Miss Sawako doesn't have to worry!
They're only after young girls!

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.520
What's that supposed
to mean, Junpei?

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:09.150
- Stay down, everyone!
- Junpei!

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.620
It's blanks!
They're firing blanks!

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:18.250
Stay calm, everyone!
We're fine!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.910
Look at that flag!

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.580
That's not the Americans!
It's the Soviets!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.510
Soviet soldiers are called "Russkies"!
They kill bears with their bare hands!

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:37.260
- Take your seats, everyone.
- Yes, ma'am.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:40.390
- Ma'am!
- Yes, what is it?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:46.100
I hear the Iwasakis and Komanos fled.
Shouldn't we run away, too?

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.190
It's all right. In times like this,
we must remain calm and collected.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.990
We mustn't panic.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.160
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.580
Miss Sawako! Look!

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.760
- It's the Russkies!
- Look at that gun!

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:12.260
Miss Sawako...

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:16.930
Everything will be fine. Stay calm.
Children, take your seats!

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.390
Focus only on me.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.680
Can you do that?

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.520
0.5...

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:41.580
Please leave the room.
We're in the middle of a lesson.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:47.040
All right, can anyone
solve this problem?

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:54.220
Junpei, then.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:57.390
Please come up to the board
and solve this problem.

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.140
Junpei?

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.770
Do you know the answer, Junpei?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.980
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.620
<What's the matter?>

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.720
What do you want?!

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.620
Thank you...

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.790
- <We're leaving.>
-

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.180
It's so fast!

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:26.850
Kanta, don't!

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.860
Junpei...

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.620
<i>The Dawn Corps</i>
<i>had been disarmed</i>

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.580
<i>and had come down</i>
<i>to the village.</i>

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:49.750
Poor devils. If they're sent to Siberia,
they're never coming home.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:53.250
The defense of the island
rests with you now.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.210
Company, stop!

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.610
They're in your hands now.

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.860
Company, march!

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:50.100
<What's this garbage?!
Your valuables! Hurry up!>

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:55.400
There's nothing left for you to take!
You people keep coming and coming!

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.690
Go away!
Go away, I said!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:11.370
First I can't fish, and now look at
what they did to the house.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.830
- Grandpa!
- Here, take good care of this.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:17.540
You can come out!

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:24.510
Mitchan!

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:29.640
- What's so funny?
- Your face is all black!

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.100
But I had to pretend
to be a man!

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:34.390
Oops! Sorry!

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:37.060
Hey!

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.690
- Uncle Hideo!
- Uncle! You're back!

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:41.860
Uncle!

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:46.360
Look at you! I go away for a
while, and you grow up on me!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.780
Where were you?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.240
Off fighting, of course!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:54.500
I come back, and Japan's nothing
but ashes. Burned to the ground.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:59.960
And when I'm finally home,
what do I find? Russians, no less!

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:01.920
What's this country coming to?

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:06.180
It's good to have you home, Hideo.
Let's celebrate with a drink.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:10.390
Oh, by the way.
I have a souvenir for you two.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.390
Really?

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:14.600
And what have we here?
Ta-dah!

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:19.480
- It's the latest train engine!
- You've never seen the real thing.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:22.440
- Where's mine?
- Play with it together.

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:26.780
You have that locomotive that
Dad bought you, remember?

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:35.000
I'm amazed you got your hands
on something like that.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:39.540
There are empty houses all over.
I found it in one of those.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.460
- You mean... you stole it?
- Welcome home, sir.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.220
W-Welcome home!

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:47.760
Good, you're all fine.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.970
- Long time no see, Big Brother!
- Hideo, you're alive...

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:54.140
- You bet! Alive and kicking!
- I'm glad to hear it.

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.390
The devil's children
have the devil's luck!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:59.560
- This man isn't dying for his country!
- Hideo!

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.360
Oh, this sake is good!

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.330
No, I'm staying.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.670
I have a duty as the island's
defense force commander.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:27.260
Face up to reality, Brother!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:31.550
Japan lost! The island's been
occupied by the Red Army!

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:34.640
We should just pack up
and leave!

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:36.730
If you want to run,
I'm not stopping you.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.520
Man, what am I gonna
do with you?

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.900
Come on, Pops!
Say something!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:45.400
A fisherman who can't fish might
as well be dead! Am I right?

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:51.450
The Soviet patrol boats won't
be out in a storm like this.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.740
This is the perfect chance
to get off the island.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:57.200
The storm is just as
dangerous for us, son.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:01.460
Do you have any other way to avoid
those patrol boats?! Damn it!

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:10.970
They say the boat
washed up this morning.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:15.260
And the Noguchis had
a little kid, too... That's terrible.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:21.020
<i>Noguchi's family fled the island</i>
<i>in the storm last night.</i>

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:24.820
<i>They were lost at sea.</i>

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:28.270
Pray silently.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.330
Be seated.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:42.250
I had planned to spend first period
today on Japanese history,

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:46.040
but the study of Japanese history has
been prohibited for the time being.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:48.130
What do we study, then?

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:52.300
Today, we will be moving a few desks
into the classroom next door.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.380
That's the lower graders' room!

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:58.600
The families of the Soviet soldiers
will be coming to the island.

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:02.650
We must vacate
this classroom.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:09.020
Are the Russkie kids
gonna study Japanese?

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:13.820
Or are we gonna have
to learn Russian?

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:29.170
What's that?

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:34.420
- It's electricity!
- Wow! The island's getting electricity?

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.470
Fly!

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.390
Junpei, look at it go!

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.480
Awesome!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.820
Fly all the way to the sky!

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.800
Who's she?

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:20.550
Excuse me, who are you?
What brings you to our house?

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.020
That book!

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:25.640
That's Dad's book!

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:28.520
Give it back!
Give back our book!

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:33.030
Hey! Open the door!
Open the door! Open the door!

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.110
- Kanta, stop!
- Open up!

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:36.990
Hey! Over here!

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:51.250
The Russkies claimed the main house.
Starting today, we're living here.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:53.050
Thanks for having us, Hana!

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.130
No way!

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.930
Why us?! Why is this
happening to us?!

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:03.270
Try some of your uncle's
special burnt rice. It's good stuff!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:09.020
- We'll run out of rice soon, though.
- Where's Mitchan?

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:12.360
She fled the island with the rest
of the workers.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.570
- I hope she's okay.
- Oh.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.660
- Mitchan's not coming back?
- I guess not.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:21.620
I brought you something amazing.
This is round two!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.210
Pretty cool, huh?

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:31.920
Amazing, huh?
And you have Uncle Hideo to thank.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.540
For round three, we'll make
it move with batteries!

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.420
- Really?
- Oh, wow!

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:38.130
Thanks, Uncle!

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:42.640
Actually, Junpei, I have
a favour to ask you.

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:47.100
At 10pm tomorrow, can you make sure
there's no Russkie boats around?

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:51.520
If there aren't, can you light a
bonfire at the top of the cape?

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:53.690
Don't let the Russkies
find out what you're doing.

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.730
I can't do that!

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:58.700
Sure you can.
You're a man, aren't you?

00:21:58.780 --> 00:21:59.860
But I...

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:04.030
We'll run out of rice if we don't do
something. We'll starve, you know?

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:08.000
Look! This was left behind by
the Takashimas when they fled.

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:13.210
It's like they're asking us to
put it to good use, don't you think?

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:18.090
Better to use the proceeds to buy rice
than let the Russkies have it, right?

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:20.670
No one will miss it, right?

00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:23.550
This will let our own
family survive.

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:25.390
Here! Special treat!

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:26.970
I'm home.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:31.440
Look at you, the war is over,
but you're busier than ever!

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:35.440
I bid you good day, young men! Toil hard
with grand ambitions in your hearts!

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:37.320
I'm counting on you!

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:41.820
Later!

00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:52.790
"Tickets, please."

00:22:56.210 --> 00:22:57.840
"Thank you, sir."

00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:00.760
- "Here!"
- "Thank you, sir."

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:09.930
"Is... this all right?"

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:15.560
"Did you bring this from
the third dimension, sir?"

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:17.520
"I'm not really sure."

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:21.030
"Your ticket is in order. We will
arrive at the Southern Cross

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:23.240
at around the third
hour tomorrow."

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:26.030
"Wow, would you look at this!

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:29.500
You could even go to the
real Heaven with this ticket!

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:33.710
And not just Heaven! This is
a free pass to go anywhere!

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.830
With this ticket, I bet you
could go wherever you wanted

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:41.090
aboard this imperfect, imaginary,
fourth dimensional galactic railroad.

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:44.550
You're one lucky fella!"

00:23:53.440 --> 00:23:55.230
I was dreaming?

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:06.450
Dad?

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:11.410
Oh, no!

00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:34.020
- Junpei!
- Ow!

00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:36.770
What are you doing
out here?

00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:39.440
Don't sneak up on me like that!
I burned myself!

00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:41.110
Beat it, kid!

00:24:41.190 --> 00:24:44.990
- You're a kid, too!
- You wet the bed!

00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:52.910
All right, fine...
Here.

00:25:00.830 --> 00:25:03.460
Don't tell Dad
about this, okay?

00:25:03.550 --> 00:25:04.840
Okay.

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:21.110
<i>♪ Red dragonfly in sunset sky ♪</i>

00:25:21.190 --> 00:25:29.700
<i>♪ I saw it one day from nanny's back ♪</i>
<i>♪ so long ago now. ♪</i>

00:25:29.860 --> 00:25:38.410
<i>♪ Picking mulberries ♪</i>
<i>♪ in mountain fields, ♪</i>

00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:46.960
<i>♪ put 'em in our little basket, ♪</i>
<i>♪ was that all but a dream? ♪</i>

00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:55.140
<i>♪ Just fifteen, ♪</i>
<i>♪ nanny went away to marry... ♪</i>

00:25:59.810 --> 00:26:02.860
Hey, that's our organ!

00:26:04.190 --> 00:26:12.820
<i>♪ Red dragonfly in sunset sky ♪</i>

00:26:12.910 --> 00:26:21.250
<i>♪ <...about her true love, ♪</i>
<i>♪ whose letters she was keeping.> ♪</i>

00:26:21.330 --> 00:26:29.630
<i>♪ Picking mulberries ♪</i>
<i>♪ in mountain fields, ♪</i>

00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:38.430
<i>♪ <...about her true love, ♪</i>
<i>♪ whose letters she was keeping.> ♪</i>

00:26:39.020 --> 00:26:46.400
<i>♪ - Red dragonfly in sunset sky... ♪</i>
<i>♪ -  ♪</i>

00:26:46.480 --> 00:26:50.940
<i>♪ - ...resting at the top of a thin pole... ♪</i>
<i>♪ -  ♪</i>

00:26:54.700 --> 00:26:56.570
We're home!

00:26:56.660 --> 00:26:58.040
Uncle!

00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:02.920
I went ahead and laid out the tracks.
It's just about finished.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.580
Will it work, Uncle?

00:27:04.670 --> 00:27:08.840
It would be a lot simpler if those
Russkies would wire up the house.

00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:11.260
Okay, all done!

00:27:11.510 --> 00:27:14.550
Okay, you two.
The train drivers sit here.

00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:21.310
Let's see, when is
the next one?

00:27:21.350 --> 00:27:24.100
Junpei, my next run
is next week!

00:27:24.190 --> 00:27:26.940
Make sure the coast
is clear, boy!

00:27:27.570 --> 00:27:30.240
- How do we work this?
- What do we do?

00:27:31.320 --> 00:27:35.030
It's simple! It'll move when
Junpei twists that dial!

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:39.120
- This makes it move?
- Wow!

00:27:39.660 --> 00:27:42.370
And now, I must away!

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:45.460
Don't try to stop me!

00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:53.180
It's moving!

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:15.530
Look!

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:17.570
It's the same kind of track!

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:23.080
- Should we?
- Yeah!

00:28:33.170 --> 00:28:35.130
We are about to depart!

00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:38.880
All aboard!

00:28:52.610 --> 00:28:55.320
Look, it's got a ribbon on it!

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:23.600
"The fine little train went on
through the fields

00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:28.060
of heavenly marsh grass
waving in the breeze,

00:29:28.230 --> 00:29:31.230
on through the faint blue light
of the triangular beacons,

00:29:31.730 --> 00:29:33.730
on by the water
of the great river..."

00:29:33.820 --> 00:29:37.230
"The fields outside looked like
a magic lantern.

00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:40.030
Triangular beacons -- a hundred,
no, a thousand..."

00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:44.530
"Campanella still whistled
lonesomely to himself,

00:29:45.030 --> 00:29:51.500
and the little girl looked off in
the same direction as Giovanni..."

00:29:51.590 --> 00:29:54.750
"And they saw that on the
shimmering edge of the Milky Way,

00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:59.130
heavenly fields of marsh grass
were glistening silver

00:29:59.220 --> 00:30:02.390
and murmuring wavelike
in the wind."

00:30:08.930 --> 00:30:13.360
May 28, 1946

00:30:14.860 --> 00:30:17.490
So, what shall we
sing today?

00:30:18.070 --> 00:30:20.490
- "The Village Blacksmith"!
- "We Are Children of the Sea"!

00:30:20.570 --> 00:30:23.200
I want to sing
"The Monkey's Palanquin"!

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:36.510
Let's do math today.

00:30:37.090 --> 00:30:41.300
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:30:41.470 --> 00:30:45.350
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:30:45.430 --> 00:30:49.560
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:53.650
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:30:54.020 --> 00:30:57.860
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:30:58.190 --> 00:31:02.070
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:31:02.160 --> 00:31:06.580
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:10.540
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:31:10.580 --> 00:31:15.000
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:31:15.080 --> 00:31:20.800
<i>♪  ♪</i>

00:31:29.050 --> 00:31:37.610
<i>♪ Red dragonfly in sunset sky ♪</i>

00:31:37.730 --> 00:31:46.160
<i>♪ I saw it one day from nanny's back ♪</i>
<i>♪ so long ago now. ♪</i>

00:31:46.410 --> 00:31:54.460
<i>♪ Picking mulberries ♪</i>
<i>♪ in mountain fields, ♪</i>

00:31:54.830 --> 00:32:03.170
<i>♪ put 'em in our little basket, ♪</i>
<i>♪ was that all but a dream? ♪</i>

00:32:05.880 --> 00:32:06.800
Got you!

00:32:06.930 --> 00:32:08.890
<Oh, crap!>

00:32:11.310 --> 00:32:13.390
Try and catch me!

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:28.410
Sorry!

00:33:03.780 --> 00:33:05.610
<i>"Ice"</i>

00:33:09.370 --> 00:33:10.320
<Tanya.>

00:33:10.450 --> 00:33:12.080
Tanya?

00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:13.910
<Yes, Tanya.>

00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:15.160
Tanya!

00:33:15.290 --> 00:33:17.710
-
- Us?

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:20.790
Giovanni.

00:33:21.210 --> 00:33:22.750
<Giovanni?>

00:33:23.590 --> 00:33:26.550
She wouldn't understand
our names in Japanese, anyway.

00:33:27.090 --> 00:33:28.170
Capanella!

00:33:28.590 --> 00:33:29.800
<Campanella?>

00:33:29.880 --> 00:33:31.220
Da, da!

00:33:31.300 --> 00:33:33.430
- Giovanni!
- Campanella!

00:33:35.180 --> 00:33:39.350
- Hey! Get off my cart!
- Sorry!

00:33:51.870 --> 00:33:54.200
Wow...

00:33:54.330 --> 00:33:55.580
Kanta, quiet!

00:33:58.540 --> 00:33:59.910
What's this?

00:34:00.460 --> 00:34:02.130
This is huge!

00:34:07.590 --> 00:34:10.090
This is Grandpa and Dad's room!

00:34:11.220 --> 00:34:13.350
And this is our room!

00:34:13.470 --> 00:34:16.220
Look at what they've
done to it...

00:34:20.650 --> 00:34:23.020
All of our things are gone...

00:34:26.190 --> 00:34:28.400
<i></i>

00:34:32.820 --> 00:34:35.530
This is our island?
It's so small...

00:34:36.290 --> 00:34:38.830
Sure you came from
a long way away.

00:34:38.950 --> 00:34:43.290
<I've moved from one place
to another all my life.>

00:35:30.300 --> 00:35:31.720
<Supper's ready.>

00:35:32.170 --> 00:35:33.970
Wow...

00:35:34.050 --> 00:35:37.050
This looks so good!

00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:40.230
Hey!

00:35:44.230 --> 00:35:45.520
<I'm home.>

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:50.820
<i>That commander,</i>
<i>he's Tanya's dad?</i>

00:35:51.150 --> 00:35:54.360
<i></i>

00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:58.320
<Let's eat!>

00:35:58.780 --> 00:36:00.990
Let's eat--

00:36:06.170 --> 00:36:08.750
- Oh, I get it!
- Here goes!

00:36:10.670 --> 00:36:11.630
Oops!

00:36:14.470 --> 00:36:15.590
That's hot!

00:36:16.680 --> 00:36:18.680
<Oh, poor thing!>

00:36:27.940 --> 00:36:29.940
<Come, dance with me!>

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:32.860
- <That's my girl!>
-

00:36:33.280 --> 00:36:36.070
<Let's dance!
Come on!>

00:36:36.200 --> 00:36:37.950
I'll dance with you!

00:36:41.530 --> 00:36:45.540
Like this! Then this!
Then this and this and this!

00:36:45.660 --> 00:36:48.630
<i>As I watched Kanta</i>
<i>dancing so happily,</i>

00:36:49.590 --> 00:36:54.380
<i>it reminded me of when</i>
<i>Mum was still alive.</i>

00:36:55.260 --> 00:37:00.760
<i>I was overcome by a warm feeling</i>
<i>that I hadn't had in a long time.</i>

00:37:05.100 --> 00:37:08.980
- Maybe I'll join Tanya's family!
- You'll what?

00:37:09.060 --> 00:37:11.940
Then I'll get to eat great food
and dance all the time!

00:37:12.030 --> 00:37:15.070
A Japanese can't become
a Russkie, dummy!

00:37:15.740 --> 00:37:18.110
Why don't you
marry Tanya, then?

00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:21.030
You like her, don't you?

00:37:21.110 --> 00:37:23.200
I... I don't. Okay?

00:37:23.660 --> 00:37:25.410
I'll marry her, then!

00:37:25.700 --> 00:37:29.000
You can't do that!
You just... can't!

00:37:40.970 --> 00:37:43.810
I'm glad you're here, Junpei!

00:37:44.560 --> 00:37:47.270
- Where's Kanta?
- He has field chores today.

00:37:47.600 --> 00:37:50.060
Too bad, I've got
some tasty treats.

00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:51.650
- Look!
- Wow!

00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:53.860
They've got everything
on the mainland.

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:56.900
I'm heading out again tonight.
I'll be counting on you!

00:37:56.990 --> 00:38:00.030
- Please, no more...
- It's for the good of the country!

00:38:00.110 --> 00:38:03.990
Endure the unendurable and
suffer the insufferable! Okay?

00:38:04.660 --> 00:38:09.160
Better hide the rice. Can't be
too careful these days.

00:38:10.460 --> 00:38:14.170
What do we have here?
Way to go, Big Bro.

00:38:14.300 --> 00:38:15.300
Oh, well.

00:38:17.250 --> 00:38:21.390
See ya. Don't forget
about tonight, little man!

00:38:24.010 --> 00:38:26.350
- Oh why me?
- Hi, fair lady!

00:38:26.430 --> 00:38:27.760
<Hello.>

00:38:34.150 --> 00:38:35.730
Zdravstvujte, Madam!

00:38:35.990 --> 00:38:38.900
<Goodness, Campa,
your Russian is excellent!>

00:38:39.440 --> 00:38:40.450
Where's Tanya?

00:38:40.570 --> 00:38:43.660
<Oh, she left with Giovanni
to pick raspberries.>

00:38:45.030 --> 00:38:46.370
With Giovanni?

00:38:48.490 --> 00:38:50.870
Not that way, Tanya!

00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:53.330
There's lots of raspberries
over this way!

00:38:53.370 --> 00:38:57.670
<We'll do that later. Look at
all these flowers! Come on!>

00:38:57.790 --> 00:39:00.880
- We're not picking raspberries?
-

00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:21.400
<No, not like that!>

00:39:37.460 --> 00:39:39.170
So pretty...

00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:41.710
"Pretty"?

00:40:11.040 --> 00:40:13.040
The ice man is out here?

00:40:13.960 --> 00:40:15.620
- <Let's go!>
- Da!

00:40:33.020 --> 00:40:33.980
That's it.

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:37.190
That should be enough.

00:40:37.730 --> 00:40:39.650
Dad?

00:40:41.730 --> 00:40:43.480
Be careful.

00:40:51.320 --> 00:40:55.500
Thank you for everything.
But you've done enough.

00:40:55.580 --> 00:41:00.000
If the Soviet soldiers find this,
it'll spell big trouble for you.

00:41:00.290 --> 00:41:02.210
Please, let me help.

00:41:03.300 --> 00:41:07.300
You can't distribute rice to
the whole village by yourself.

00:41:07.380 --> 00:41:10.100
But it's only a matter of time
before we're discovered.

00:41:10.390 --> 00:41:12.220
I mustn't ruin your life.

00:41:12.350 --> 00:41:13.060
No!

00:41:16.850 --> 00:41:19.770
Being useful to you
makes me happy, Tatsuo.

00:41:19.860 --> 00:41:23.520
You know my feelings for you
ever since we were little.

00:41:23.610 --> 00:41:26.200
I won't go.

00:41:31.530 --> 00:41:33.160
Let's go!

00:41:42.670 --> 00:41:46.010
Listen, Tanya. You can't tell
anyone what we saw here today.

00:41:48.130 --> 00:41:49.340
<i></i>

00:41:51.510 --> 00:41:53.970
- Promise me!
- <i></i>

00:41:54.520 --> 00:41:57.230
- Go home, then!
- <i></i>

00:41:57.520 --> 00:42:01.610
Go home! Go! Go!

00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:07.440
<No. I'll sit here until I rot, and the
animals will feed on my carcass.>

00:42:07.940 --> 00:42:10.070
What am I gonna do?

00:42:16.750 --> 00:42:18.540
<What's the matter, Giovanni?>

00:42:19.040 --> 00:42:21.210
I'm seeing if there are any
Russkie boats around.

00:42:22.040 --> 00:42:23.790
Soviet. Boats.

00:42:24.290 --> 00:42:25.630
<Boats?>

00:42:26.260 --> 00:42:30.880
<No, everyone is celebrating tonight.
There won't be a patrol.>

00:42:31.180 --> 00:42:33.390
Boats. No come.

00:42:33.470 --> 00:42:34.890
Really?

00:42:34.970 --> 00:42:35.970
Really.

00:42:44.230 --> 00:42:47.440
There's a blanket in my bag.
Use it if you want.

00:43:14.890 --> 00:43:17.310
Give it back! Give it back!

00:43:30.820 --> 00:43:31.700
Draw you?

00:44:19.240 --> 00:44:25.750
<i>I wished that time would stand still</i>
<i>and we could stay that way forever.</i>

00:44:36.510 --> 00:44:38.510
That's Uncle Hideo's boat!

00:45:09.130 --> 00:45:13.210
Junpei... Where did you go
with Tanya today?

00:45:17.050 --> 00:45:20.010
Come on, what were you
doing with Tanya?

00:45:28.730 --> 00:45:31.020
- What's the big idea?!
- Uncle!

00:45:31.270 --> 00:45:32.940
Are you trying
to get me killed?!

00:45:33.570 --> 00:45:35.570
Thank goodness, you're alive!

00:45:35.740 --> 00:45:38.950
Of course I am! It'll take
more than that to knock me out!

00:45:39.030 --> 00:45:41.990
I'm sorry, Tanya said
there was no patrol, so I--

00:45:42.070 --> 00:45:43.580
- "Tanya"?
- Yeah.

00:45:44.330 --> 00:45:47.460
Oh, that girl in the main house?
Now I see.

00:45:47.870 --> 00:45:50.620
She's the Soviet commander's daughter.
Be careful, you hear?

00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:53.710
Beware a pretty face, kiddo!

00:45:53.790 --> 00:45:56.210
What? She's not like that, I--

00:45:56.510 --> 00:45:58.630
- By the way, is your dad around?
- He's not home.

00:45:58.720 --> 00:46:00.930
He left real early
this morning!

00:46:01.430 --> 00:46:04.310
He's an early riser, my brother...

00:46:05.060 --> 00:46:08.980
- What is it, Junpei?
- Something's been bothering me.

00:46:09.190 --> 00:46:09.810
Like what?

00:46:09.930 --> 00:46:12.770
Dad and Miss Sawako
were at the cave, and--

00:46:12.860 --> 00:46:16.990
What? What about the cave?
Why were they together at the cave?

00:46:20.320 --> 00:46:24.990
That's the Dawn Corps' emergency stores!
You can't just help yourself to them!

00:46:25.080 --> 00:46:30.170
They belong to all of us. We need
them to keep from starving.

00:46:30.250 --> 00:46:32.040
They mustn't fall into
the Soviets' hands!

00:46:32.380 --> 00:46:36.250
Don't be stupid! I'll turn that
rice into money on the mainland.

00:46:36.340 --> 00:46:38.760
- That's the smart move!
- I won't let you!

00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:40.300
Try to stop me!

00:46:41.970 --> 00:46:44.720
Enough. The folks next door
will hear.

00:46:45.140 --> 00:46:49.600
I get it, you've been getting the rice
to the villagers through Sawako.

00:46:49.680 --> 00:46:53.810
- Distributing it from the school...
- Not another word, I mean it.

00:46:53.900 --> 00:46:56.110
So, are you two an item?

00:47:02.990 --> 00:47:06.070
The war is over, Bro.

00:47:07.330 --> 00:47:10.830
It's time to face up
to reality.

00:47:14.130 --> 00:47:15.460
Hideo...

00:47:24.430 --> 00:47:28.220
July 16, 1946

00:47:31.100 --> 00:47:32.980
It's Sawako!
It's me, Sawako!

00:47:34.060 --> 00:47:36.690
- It's Miss Sawako!
- What's going on?

00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:40.400
Please open up!
Open the door!

00:47:42.570 --> 00:47:45.240
- It's Hideo, he--
- What about Hideo?

00:47:45.740 --> 00:47:51.200
Hideo was trying to smuggle out
the rice, and he was caught by a patrol!

00:47:51.960 --> 00:47:53.210
If he talks--

00:47:54.580 --> 00:47:56.380
Tatsuo, wait!

00:47:57.210 --> 00:47:59.210
Look after the boys, Sawako!

00:47:59.340 --> 00:48:00.710
Dad!

00:48:05.430 --> 00:48:08.470
<i>She's the Soviet commander's daughter.</i>
<i>Be careful, you hear?</i>

00:48:14.850 --> 00:48:18.230
Don't go, Dad!

00:48:38.170 --> 00:48:39.170
Dad...

00:48:45.090 --> 00:48:47.760
Dad... Dad!

00:48:54.020 --> 00:48:54.940
Dad!

00:49:06.240 --> 00:49:09.330
Dad! Dad!

00:49:09.450 --> 00:49:12.370
Dad!!

00:49:17.580 --> 00:49:18.790
Tanya!

00:49:20.750 --> 00:49:24.800
<Giovanni? What's the matter?>
Tanya! My dad's been taken!

00:49:24.970 --> 00:49:27.420
<What? Speak slowly.>

00:49:28.260 --> 00:49:30.260
Tanya, did you tell them?

00:49:31.930 --> 00:49:37.730
Your father arrested my dad!
Because you talked!

00:49:38.190 --> 00:49:40.020
<i></i>

00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:44.730
Liar! How come your father
knew about the cave, then?!

00:49:45.030 --> 00:49:46.660
-
- You told him!

00:49:48.570 --> 00:49:49.740
<i></i>

00:49:57.080 --> 00:50:00.500
<i></i>

00:50:01.460 --> 00:50:05.460
<What's the matter, pumpkin?
Wasn't that Giovanni I heard outside?>

00:50:08.930 --> 00:50:11.930
But they took my dad...

00:50:17.020 --> 00:50:20.730
Dad's been arrested
by the Russkies...

00:50:34.200 --> 00:50:37.450
"'What kind of light is that?

00:50:39.290 --> 00:50:43.920
What can they be burning
to get such red flames?'

00:50:45.590 --> 00:50:47.550
asked Giovanni.

00:50:48.720 --> 00:50:56.180
'It's the Fire of Scorpius,' said
Campanella, again referring to his map.

00:50:58.850 --> 00:51:04.440
'O God, look into my heart,'
prayed the scorpion.

00:51:06.190 --> 00:51:09.320
'Instead of throwing my life away
in vain like this,

00:51:09.400 --> 00:51:17.830
grant that my body be used for
the true welfare of all.'

00:51:20.460 --> 00:51:25.790
And then the scorpion's body
suddenly broke up

00:51:26.880 --> 00:51:29.250
into beautiful crimson flames,

00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:34.180
and he was placed in the heavens
to light the darkness of the night.

00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:38.350
My father said that the fire
burns to this very day.'"

00:52:22.980 --> 00:52:26.480
September 25, 1947

00:52:29.570 --> 00:52:31.740
Genzo! Genzo!

00:52:33.150 --> 00:52:33.950
Genzo!

00:52:34.030 --> 00:52:35.570
What's all the ruckus?

00:52:36.910 --> 00:52:41.490
Everyone on the island is being
sent back to the mainland!

00:52:44.080 --> 00:52:47.420
They say to gather at the harbor
with only what we can carry!

00:52:49.210 --> 00:52:51.040
- Grandpa?
- Right.

00:52:51.550 --> 00:52:53.920
- Will we be allowed back?
-

00:52:56.970 --> 00:53:00.930
Put on every piece of clothing
you can and wait outside.

00:53:01.010 --> 00:53:04.060
Miss Sawako will
be here for you soon.

00:53:08.190 --> 00:53:10.060
Here you go.

00:53:11.320 --> 00:53:14.280
You are a big boy now, Kanta.
Grin and bear it.

00:53:14.360 --> 00:53:15.900
It's fine.

00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:23.120
I'll catch up with you soon.
Until then, look after Kanta.

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:25.580
You can count on me, Grandpa.

00:53:26.250 --> 00:53:28.040
Is everyone ready?

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:29.370
Miss Sawako!

00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:32.250
Everyone's heading to the wharf.
We have to hurry.

00:53:32.340 --> 00:53:33.380
Right.

00:53:33.460 --> 00:53:36.970
- And your grandfather?
- He said to go, he'll catch up.

00:53:37.510 --> 00:53:38.430
Uncle Genzo?

00:53:43.180 --> 00:53:44.220
Uncle Genzo?

00:53:44.310 --> 00:53:47.520
I'm an old man who doesn't
have many years left.

00:53:47.600 --> 00:53:52.440
I'm sorry, but look after
Junpei and Kanta for me.

00:53:56.240 --> 00:54:03.080
With us fishermen, we live,
we eat, we fish, and we die.

00:54:03.160 --> 00:54:08.920
We're content with that.
That's a life we're proud of.

00:54:32.940 --> 00:54:34.780
Hey! Miss Sawako!

00:54:35.070 --> 00:54:37.440
- Kanta!
- Miss Sawako!

00:54:37.530 --> 00:54:39.400
Junpei! Kanta!

00:54:39.700 --> 00:54:41.280
It's Uncle!

00:54:41.410 --> 00:54:43.240
- Hideo!
- You're okay!

00:54:43.370 --> 00:54:46.580
You are speaking to an
indestructible wandering crow!

00:54:46.660 --> 00:54:48.500
They interrogated you, right?

00:54:48.580 --> 00:54:51.920
Sure, but your uncle
doesn't break easily.

00:54:52.420 --> 00:54:54.750
Your dad is so stubborn.

00:54:54.880 --> 00:54:58.710
If he'd played along,
they would've let him go.

00:55:03.640 --> 00:55:05.100
It was you?!

00:55:05.850 --> 00:55:09.350
Hey, It's not like I
sold him out or anything.

00:55:10.350 --> 00:55:12.350
I tried to help him.

00:55:12.900 --> 00:55:16.060
Oh, well.
Say, where's Pops?

00:55:26.780 --> 00:55:29.370
<i>I asked Miss Sawako</i>
<i>about him afterwards.</i>

00:55:30.830 --> 00:55:33.460
<i>She said my grandpa</i>
<i>had made up his mind</i>

00:55:34.500 --> 00:55:37.420
<i>that his last moments</i>
<i>would be on the sea.</i>

00:55:42.800 --> 00:55:46.850
I wonder if we'll ever be able
to come back to the island?

00:55:58.610 --> 00:56:00.860
Junpei! Look!

00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:03.570
Isn't that Tanya?

00:56:07.410 --> 00:56:09.330
Tanya...

00:56:10.290 --> 00:56:13.910
I'm sorry.
Tanya, I'm so sorry.

00:56:15.460 --> 00:56:16.500
Tanya!

00:56:21.090 --> 00:56:23.420
Tanya! Tanya!

00:56:30.850 --> 00:56:36.850
<i>And that was how</i>
<i>we left the island.</i>

00:56:53.080 --> 00:56:58.000
- Haven't we reached Japan yet?
- We must be almost there.

00:57:00.710 --> 00:57:02.340
It's freezing...

00:57:04.720 --> 00:57:06.840
Need the loo...

00:57:07.840 --> 00:57:11.140
Give her back!
Give back my baby!

00:57:11.390 --> 00:57:12.890
Please!

00:57:14.350 --> 00:57:16.390
Please! Give her back!

00:57:16.480 --> 00:57:18.980
- <We're not allowed!>
- <It's the orders!>

00:57:19.400 --> 00:57:22.940
The baby's dead.
There's nothing else to do.

00:57:23.030 --> 00:57:25.400
No!

00:57:28.450 --> 00:57:29.740
Yasuko!

00:57:29.870 --> 00:57:32.910
Yasuko! Yasuko!

00:57:37.410 --> 00:57:42.750
<i>Day after day,</i>
<i>the storm raged on.</i>

00:57:50.760 --> 00:57:54.810
October 3, 1947

00:58:13.660 --> 00:58:15.410
What is this place?

00:58:15.500 --> 00:58:18.870
This doesn't seem like
Nemuro or Hakodate.

00:58:31.760 --> 00:58:34.010
This isn't Japan!

00:58:38.390 --> 00:58:44.980
Sugar! Sugar!
Who wants sugar?

00:58:45.070 --> 00:58:46.690
It's sweet!

00:58:46.900 --> 00:58:50.650
I'm beat...
This is so heavy...

00:58:51.030 --> 00:58:52.280
Kanta...

00:58:52.820 --> 00:58:54.620
Are you okay, Kanta?

00:58:55.080 --> 00:58:56.490
Sweet sugar, sir!

00:58:56.950 --> 00:58:59.040
Wait here!

00:59:00.500 --> 00:59:01.920
Three sugars, please!

00:59:03.420 --> 00:59:04.920
Thanks.

00:59:06.250 --> 00:59:07.840
Sugar!

00:59:07.920 --> 00:59:09.800
Turn those frowns upside-down!

00:59:10.630 --> 00:59:12.260
Wow, it's sugar!

00:59:12.380 --> 00:59:14.010
Thanks, Uncle!

00:59:14.970 --> 00:59:16.800
A token of my love, milady!

00:59:17.680 --> 00:59:19.180
Be my guest!

00:59:24.860 --> 00:59:27.070
The bottom is sand!

00:59:27.190 --> 00:59:29.530
Sand? That little crook!

00:59:29.650 --> 00:59:32.200
Where'd he go?!
Come back here!

00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:48.340
- It's so fast!
- It's so big!

00:59:50.590 --> 00:59:54.590
<i>For the first time in our lives,</i>
<i>we saw a real train.</i>

00:59:54.760 --> 00:59:58.470
- Wow!
- That was the real thing!

01:00:03.310 --> 01:00:08.230
<i>The internment camp was a</i>
<i>primary school at the top of a hill.</i>

01:00:08.860 --> 01:00:10.570
Hey, no cutting!

01:00:11.780 --> 01:00:13.150
This is all?

01:00:14.150 --> 01:00:16.120
It's gross...

01:00:20.410 --> 01:00:21.870
Boo!

01:00:24.330 --> 01:00:25.040
Ta-dah!

01:00:25.170 --> 01:00:28.580
- Wow, biscuits!
- Eat up!

01:00:28.670 --> 01:00:31.220
- Look, everybody!
- Let's share them.

01:00:31.300 --> 01:00:35.430
Apparently, we're in Maoka,
in western Karafuto.

01:00:35.510 --> 01:00:36.340
Oh.

01:00:36.470 --> 01:00:39.760
Everybody from the islands
is being rounded up here.

01:00:39.850 --> 01:00:42.930
Then a ship from Japan
will come pick us up, they say.

01:00:43.310 --> 01:00:45.650
So we'll be able to
go back to Japan?

01:00:45.940 --> 01:00:49.270
I'm not so sure. Something tells
me it won't be that simple.

01:00:49.360 --> 01:00:50.480
Why?

01:01:03.750 --> 01:01:06.960
- Junpei, I'm so cold...
- Kanta?

01:01:07.040 --> 01:01:08.540
I'm so cold...

01:01:08.710 --> 01:01:10.000
Everything will be okay.

01:01:11.000 --> 01:01:13.510
I wonder what Tanya
is up to?

01:01:13.710 --> 01:01:17.890
With everyone gone,
she must be lonely.

01:01:31.480 --> 01:01:33.900
-
-

01:01:34.440 --> 01:01:41.490
<i>Every day, they took the adults</i>
<i>deep into the mountains to cut wood.</i>

01:01:42.080 --> 01:01:46.160
<i>It was back-breaking work,</i>

01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:52.500
<i>and some of them got hurt</i>
<i>or got sick from the cold.</i>

01:02:05.140 --> 01:02:06.230
Kanta...

01:02:10.850 --> 01:02:14.860
Where is Dad?

01:02:15.150 --> 01:02:17.780
Don't worry.
I'm sure he's fine.

01:02:18.240 --> 01:02:21.450
Miss Sawako...
Were you and Dad--

01:02:22.200 --> 01:02:24.200
Forget it.

01:02:26.540 --> 01:02:29.370
I care a great deal
for your father.

01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:35.590
He knew that he would be arrested
if he went to the cave.

01:02:36.090 --> 01:02:38.710
He felt it was his duty.

01:02:39.590 --> 01:02:43.180
I wonder if Dad has turned
into the Fire of Scorpius...

01:02:44.560 --> 01:02:48.390
Well, I--
I'm sure that he has.

01:02:49.850 --> 01:02:52.520
Your father lived
his life for others.

01:02:53.360 --> 01:02:55.610
And for you boys.

01:02:57.150 --> 01:02:59.280
I have to be strong now, too.

01:03:01.990 --> 01:03:04.820
You gave me the courage
to go on, Junpei.

01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:25.430
It's so cold...

01:03:25.550 --> 01:03:29.430
Once they've taken everyone in
the girls' school, it'll be our turn.

01:03:29.560 --> 01:03:33.020
- Hang in there.
- I can't...

01:03:38.320 --> 01:03:41.450
I have great news!
I found out where Tatsuo is!

01:03:41.570 --> 01:03:43.280
- Dad is alive?!
- Really?!

01:03:43.530 --> 01:03:46.950
At the logging camp, I met a guy
who's housed in the same place!

01:03:47.450 --> 01:03:50.160
He says he's in the
prison camp to the north!

01:03:50.290 --> 01:03:54.460
Beyond those mountains!
It's just a stone's throw from here!

01:03:54.630 --> 01:03:56.960
- Thank goodness...
- Kanta!

01:03:58.550 --> 01:04:00.670
He didn't get sent to Siberia!

01:04:00.760 --> 01:04:03.510
He said he's just past
those mountains, right?

01:04:17.270 --> 01:04:20.280
- Did he mean those mountains?
- I guess.

01:04:22.730 --> 01:04:26.240
Junpei, I'm gonna
go see Dad.

01:04:29.240 --> 01:04:31.500
- Let's go!
- How?

01:04:31.660 --> 01:04:35.040
We'd have to go way beyond
that train's final stop.

01:04:35.170 --> 01:04:37.040
I don't care!

01:04:37.170 --> 01:04:40.300
See? You have to
get better first.

01:04:40.710 --> 01:04:43.800
I'd get better real quick
if I saw Dad!

01:04:43.920 --> 01:04:45.220
Still...

01:04:45.300 --> 01:04:49.010
Don't you want to ever
see Dad again?!

01:04:51.890 --> 01:04:53.730
But how?

01:04:58.020 --> 01:05:00.570
Let's take the
Galactic Railroad there!

01:05:00.690 --> 01:05:02.570
Kanta...

01:05:09.240 --> 01:05:11.450
I'm freezing...

01:05:17.630 --> 01:05:19.460
What's the matter?

01:05:19.590 --> 01:05:21.130
Those kids!

01:05:34.020 --> 01:05:35.060
Kanta!

01:05:36.060 --> 01:05:38.520
- Kanta! Hurry!
- Junpei!

01:05:48.030 --> 01:05:49.400
Go on!

01:05:56.370 --> 01:05:59.920
Real trains sure are bumpy, huh?

01:06:00.630 --> 01:06:03.420
This will take us to Dad
in no time flat!

01:06:44.880 --> 01:06:47.420
Kanta, are you okay?

01:07:00.140 --> 01:07:03.440
This thing cost me
everything I had, damn it!

01:07:03.520 --> 01:07:04.980
Will we catch them?

01:07:05.060 --> 01:07:07.190
The end of the train line
is just ahead.

01:07:17.120 --> 01:07:20.290
- I'm so sorry...
- Don't worry about it.

01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:23.130
- Thanks.
- Are you okay?

01:07:23.250 --> 01:07:24.210
I'm fine...

01:07:32.380 --> 01:07:36.890
If they got off the train and walked,
they should be around here.

01:07:45.860 --> 01:07:47.650
You two idiots!

01:07:48.780 --> 01:07:49.990
Uncle Hideo!

01:07:50.490 --> 01:07:53.570
If I were a Soviet soldier,
you'd be dead right now!

01:07:53.660 --> 01:07:55.660
What were you thinking?!

01:07:56.450 --> 01:07:57.950
We're sorry.

01:07:58.030 --> 01:08:00.580
Come on, we're going back!

01:08:01.460 --> 01:08:03.880
No! I'm gonna see Dad!

01:08:03.880 --> 01:08:05.210
Kanta!

01:08:06.920 --> 01:08:08.170
No! Put me down!

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:11.250
You dumb kid! Even if you
do see him, then what?!

01:08:11.340 --> 01:08:13.050
I wanna see him!

01:08:13.180 --> 01:08:17.300
We're going to see Dad!
Our minds are made up!

01:08:17.390 --> 01:08:18.390
Ow!

01:08:21.060 --> 01:08:24.520
You stubborn little kids!
That's the last thing he wants!

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:27.480
No! We're seeing him,
no matter what!

01:08:30.490 --> 01:08:32.280
Of all the stupid...

01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:46.080
Hey!

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:48.500
Come back here!

01:08:49.130 --> 01:08:53.510
Uncle, please!
We want to see Dad!

01:08:53.930 --> 01:08:54.550
No!

01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:59.090
I can't let you two die
in a place like this!

01:08:59.180 --> 01:09:01.430
No, I want to see him!

01:09:01.520 --> 01:09:05.650
You're the one who said he was
just a stone's throw away!

01:09:09.730 --> 01:09:13.690
Fine, I said that.
But I didn't mean it literally!

01:09:15.320 --> 01:09:18.280
What am I gonna do
with you two?

01:09:18.370 --> 01:09:22.700
Come on, Sawako!
Talk sense into them!

01:09:24.460 --> 01:09:26.910
- I'm going, too.
- Wha--?

01:09:27.290 --> 01:09:31.630
Please, let us go.
I want to see Tatsuo, too.

01:09:32.670 --> 01:09:35.680
Besides, we're closer to his camp
than we are to ours.

01:09:36.340 --> 01:09:38.850
Guards might be
on our trail, too.

01:09:43.100 --> 01:09:45.270
Oh, for crying out loud...

01:09:46.560 --> 01:09:51.150
At a time like this,
what's a man supposed to do?

01:09:51.730 --> 01:09:54.280
Could one of you tell me?

01:09:55.700 --> 01:09:58.360
- Thank you, Uncle!
- Thank you!

01:09:58.450 --> 01:10:00.620
- Cut it out, damn it!
- Thank you!

01:10:00.700 --> 01:10:03.830
I wish I were as popular
as my brother...

01:10:03.910 --> 01:10:05.910
Man, you two are heavy...

01:10:28.060 --> 01:10:29.560
What's that?

01:10:31.820 --> 01:10:33.560
A fortification?

01:10:40.990 --> 01:10:42.950
It's so warm...

01:10:44.410 --> 01:10:46.490
Thank goodness
for this pillbox.

01:10:47.920 --> 01:10:50.920
- I'd love a hot bath right about now.
- Here.

01:10:53.170 --> 01:10:54.880
Boy, this warms you right up!

01:11:17.360 --> 01:11:18.360
Hideo!

01:11:19.900 --> 01:11:21.610
Wow, it's freezing!

01:11:24.490 --> 01:11:26.200
What's up, Sawako?

01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:28.660
- Soldiers.
- What?

01:11:29.290 --> 01:11:31.620
Looks like they found
where I hid the car.

01:11:31.920 --> 01:11:34.750
- Sawako, wake up the boys!
- Right!

01:11:35.590 --> 01:11:37.090
What's wrong?

01:11:37.670 --> 01:11:41.550
While I keep them distracted, you
and the boys make a break for it.

01:11:42.510 --> 01:11:45.300
Here's the address of our
relatives on the mainland.

01:11:45.550 --> 01:11:48.140
Junpei, look after Kanta
and Sawako, you hear?

01:11:48.260 --> 01:11:49.760
Uncle...

01:11:51.140 --> 01:11:52.480
Hideo...

01:11:52.560 --> 01:11:57.400
If I were a Soviet soldier, I could give
you a big bear hug to say goodbye.

01:11:59.270 --> 01:12:01.700
Maybe I will anyway.

01:12:07.870 --> 01:12:11.080
Sawako. I always
loved you.

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:17.210
I hope you get to see
your dad, Kanta.

01:12:17.290 --> 01:12:18.500
Uncle...

01:12:18.630 --> 01:12:21.050
Hey, I'm an indestructible,
wandering crow!

01:12:21.670 --> 01:12:24.680
And now, everyone,
I bid you farewell.

01:12:30.890 --> 01:12:33.220
- <Look, look!>
- <Halt!>

01:12:33.560 --> 01:12:34.730
<Halt!>

01:12:34.850 --> 01:12:36.230
<Stop, or we'll shoot!>

01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:38.400
<Shoot! Shoot him!>

01:12:59.210 --> 01:13:00.800
Let's go, boys.

01:13:33.540 --> 01:13:38.210
Just a little further, Kanta. Hold on
until the settlement up ahead.

01:13:39.000 --> 01:13:40.460
Kanta...

01:13:40.540 --> 01:13:44.010
"Wow, would you look at this!

01:13:44.090 --> 01:13:48.180
You could even go to the
real Heaven with this ticket!

01:13:48.260 --> 01:13:53.180
And not just Heaven! This is
a free pass to go anywhere!"

01:13:53.680 --> 01:13:57.520
Kanta, this is a sign that
we can make it to see Dad!

01:13:57.600 --> 01:13:58.810
We're almost there!

01:13:59.980 --> 01:14:00.690
Junpei...

01:14:19.210 --> 01:14:21.330
This is the Galactic Railroad,
isn't it?

01:14:21.420 --> 01:14:23.590
I have this free pass
to go anywhere!

01:14:23.670 --> 01:14:26.300
Please take me to where
my father is!

01:14:28.300 --> 01:14:29.550
Please!

01:14:32.470 --> 01:14:35.220
Please! Let us on board!

01:14:38.890 --> 01:14:40.690
Please let us on!

01:14:42.770 --> 01:14:45.230
Let us on, please!

01:15:07.300 --> 01:15:13.140
Eat this and go.
<i></i>

01:15:13.430 --> 01:15:15.100
Thank you so much.

01:15:17.350 --> 01:15:21.060
About that matter we discussed.
I do hope we can count on you.

01:15:21.440 --> 01:15:22.690
<i></i>

01:15:26.570 --> 01:15:30.740
<i></i>

01:15:46.880 --> 01:15:48.260
It's so warm...

01:15:49.340 --> 01:15:50.590
Junpei.

01:15:51.090 --> 01:15:53.260
Take a look
out that window.

01:16:27.090 --> 01:16:29.750
- What's this?
- My end of the bargain.

01:16:30.170 --> 01:16:36.340
<i></i>

01:16:38.220 --> 01:16:39.850
Thank you so much!

01:16:45.060 --> 01:16:46.400
Junpei!

01:16:47.940 --> 01:16:50.400
<i>"Wait here tomorrow at midnight.</i>
<i>-T"</i>

01:16:50.530 --> 01:16:52.360
Dad...!

01:16:55.360 --> 01:16:58.370
<i>"Wait here tomorrow at midnight.</i>
<i>-T"</i>

01:17:11.250 --> 01:17:15.630
<i>That day was the</i>
<i>Russian New Year.</i>

01:17:16.090 --> 01:17:18.390
<i>The night of their</i>
<i>Yolka Festival.</i>

01:17:18.470 --> 01:17:20.050
Junpei...

01:17:33.860 --> 01:17:37.950
<i>♪ <A mail troika dashes ♪</i>
<i>♪ along the frozen Mother Volga...> ♪</i>

01:17:38.030 --> 01:17:40.280
<Hey, cool it!
We'll get in trouble!>

01:17:40.370 --> 01:17:43.870
<Relax! The Commandant
will overlook it today!>

01:17:44.460 --> 01:17:54.210
<i>♪ <The coachman hums a sad tune ♪</i>
<i>♪ and shakes his head...> ♪</i>

01:18:04.100 --> 01:18:07.430
<Hey, come down here
and drink with us!>

01:18:17.200 --> 01:18:18.700
There!

01:18:22.790 --> 01:18:24.290
No, wait!

01:18:26.830 --> 01:18:28.120
It's Dad!

01:18:28.870 --> 01:18:30.500
Kanta! Kanta!

01:18:35.670 --> 01:18:36.880
Dad!

01:18:37.880 --> 01:18:41.220
What were you thinking?!
What if you're caught?!

01:18:41.880 --> 01:18:44.930
It's not safe here!
Go back this instant!

01:18:46.310 --> 01:18:47.930
Go back.

01:18:49.270 --> 01:18:51.480
Go back right now!

01:19:01.740 --> 01:19:03.370
Junpei!

01:19:04.240 --> 01:19:06.620
- Kanta!
- Dad!

01:19:09.460 --> 01:19:13.210
Thank you.
I'm so glad you came.

01:19:13.340 --> 01:19:14.590
I'm so glad!

01:19:16.210 --> 01:19:19.130
We came on the
Galactic Railroad!

01:19:20.380 --> 01:19:23.850
You did?
You did, did you?

01:19:24.560 --> 01:19:26.060
Dad!

01:19:28.890 --> 01:19:30.020
Junpei!

01:19:30.890 --> 01:19:32.940
Dad!

01:19:33.060 --> 01:19:34.270
Kanta!

01:19:42.570 --> 01:19:44.110
Dad!

01:19:44.910 --> 01:19:51.580
Wait for me! I'll come
home alive, no matter what!

01:20:04.300 --> 01:20:11.100
Thank you, Sawako.
Please look after the boys.

01:20:15.190 --> 01:20:16.820
I will.

01:20:30.990 --> 01:20:33.080
Dad...

01:20:33.960 --> 01:20:35.540
Let's go.

01:20:44.300 --> 01:20:45.550
Kanta!

01:20:48.470 --> 01:20:50.390
- Kanta!
- Kanta!

01:20:51.390 --> 01:20:52.520
Kanta!

01:20:53.350 --> 01:20:55.560
- Kanta! Kanta!
- Are you all right, Kanta?

01:20:55.690 --> 01:20:56.900
Kanta!

01:21:04.070 --> 01:21:06.110
<Tomorrow? Then...>

01:21:06.410 --> 01:21:08.070
<Yes. Of course.>

01:21:08.200 --> 01:21:09.660
Kanta...

01:21:11.660 --> 01:21:13.160
<Here.>

01:21:27.010 --> 01:21:29.430
-
-

01:21:47.650 --> 01:21:53.660
Kanta! We're going home!
We're going back to Japan!

01:21:54.200 --> 01:21:56.000
<i></i>

01:21:56.290 --> 01:22:01.210
Can't you see that he's sick?
Be kind and let them talk.

01:22:05.760 --> 01:22:09.010
The stars are so pretty...

01:22:10.430 --> 01:22:14.520
Are we riding
the Galactic Railroad?

01:22:14.850 --> 01:22:19.730
That's right! We're Giovanni
and Campanella!

01:22:19.810 --> 01:22:21.810
You and me,
together forever!

01:22:23.150 --> 01:22:27.610
Look, Kanta! The Indian and
the Bird Catcher are here, too!

01:22:28.190 --> 01:22:32.200
I can see the Southern Cross
and the big Coalsack!

01:22:34.580 --> 01:22:36.410
Junpei...

01:22:38.410 --> 01:22:41.580
Am I gonna die?

01:22:41.790 --> 01:22:47.710
No way! You're not
gonna die, not here!

01:22:49.840 --> 01:22:54.390
We have this magic ticket to go
wherever we want, remember?

01:22:54.890 --> 01:22:57.980
See, Kanta? It's a ticket
for the Galactic Railroad!

01:22:59.310 --> 01:23:01.360
It is...

01:23:01.850 --> 01:23:08.320
It's a magic ticket that will let you go
anywhere you want in the whole universe!

01:23:10.280 --> 01:23:13.950
Kanta, let's go home to Japan.

01:23:14.620 --> 01:23:18.200
We'll head straight home and
eat a whole bunch of tasty food!

01:23:19.540 --> 01:23:23.130
We can do anything.
What do you want to be, Kanta?

01:23:24.380 --> 01:23:28.510
I know! A conductor on the
Galactic Railroad, right?

01:23:28.590 --> 01:23:30.590
An airplane pilot?

01:23:31.050 --> 01:23:34.010
You could even be a sailor or
own a toy store or a bookshop!

01:23:34.140 --> 01:23:36.140
You can be anything!

01:23:37.100 --> 01:23:40.690
When you grow up, you can even
get married and have kids!

01:23:41.560 --> 01:23:44.520
You can ride in cars,
sing songs,

01:23:44.650 --> 01:23:47.730
go swimming, see movies,
go fishing!

01:23:54.410 --> 01:23:57.620
You're right, Junpei...

01:23:58.330 --> 01:24:00.540
I can see a light...

01:24:01.910 --> 01:24:04.580
I wonder if it's
the final stop?

01:24:04.750 --> 01:24:07.590
No! Don't go there!

01:24:08.880 --> 01:24:12.010
I can see a lovely field...

01:24:13.510 --> 01:24:16.930
It's such a lovely field...

01:24:18.180 --> 01:24:20.890
This has to be

01:24:21.730 --> 01:24:26.190
the final stop on the line.

01:24:26.480 --> 01:24:28.110
Dummy!

01:24:28.400 --> 01:24:31.820
We're supposed to stick
together forever!

01:24:31.900 --> 01:24:33.740
Right, Kanta?!

01:24:36.950 --> 01:24:38.370
Kanta?

01:24:41.370 --> 01:24:42.460
Kanta!

01:24:44.880 --> 01:24:46.460
Kanta...

01:24:59.180 --> 01:25:00.930
Kanta!

01:25:48.480 --> 01:25:50.150
Hey!

01:25:51.900 --> 01:25:53.570
- Uncle?!
- Hideo!

01:25:53.900 --> 01:25:56.820
I'm an indestructible,
wandering crow, you know!

01:25:56.900 --> 01:25:58.740
Hideo, what happened
to your leg?

01:25:58.830 --> 01:26:02.450
The Russkies are rusty,
but their bullets have bite.

01:26:03.250 --> 01:26:05.660
Did you see Tatsuo?

01:26:05.830 --> 01:26:07.330
Hey, Kanta.
What's the matter?

01:26:12.170 --> 01:26:15.760
He didn't make it, huh?
Damn.

01:26:20.470 --> 01:26:23.350
Come on, let's all
go home together.

01:26:23.560 --> 01:26:24.600
Honey!

01:26:28.810 --> 01:26:31.480
If you die, you get thrown
by the wayside.

01:26:32.520 --> 01:26:34.150
Junpei! Prop up Kanta!

01:26:36.030 --> 01:26:39.530
Make it look like he's alive!
Talk to him! About anything!

01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:43.120
There has to be something!
Think!

01:26:43.410 --> 01:26:47.910
I know! Kenji Miyazawa!
Wasn't the Galactic Railroad born here?

01:26:48.040 --> 01:26:50.710
It was! Kenji Miyazawa
came to Karafuto

01:26:50.790 --> 01:26:53.710
because he wanted to talk
to his late sister.

01:26:53.920 --> 01:26:57.630
The Galactic Railroad was his way of
communicating with his sister in space!

01:26:57.960 --> 01:27:01.720
That story was born right here!
On this very spot!

01:27:02.140 --> 01:27:03.390
Junpei!

01:27:06.100 --> 01:27:09.440
Kanta. Let's go home together.

01:27:10.270 --> 01:27:12.060
Back to Japan!

01:27:14.320 --> 01:27:17.820
"It was at that precise moment
that it happened.

01:27:18.240 --> 01:27:21.400
In the far distance of the
Milky Way's downstream course,

01:27:21.490 --> 01:27:26.990
a cross, bejeweled with bright
orange and blue lights,

01:27:28.330 --> 01:27:32.960
appeared, standing shimmering
in the midst of the river."

01:27:34.420 --> 01:27:38.170
Kanta, can you see it?
Can you see the cross?

01:27:45.010 --> 01:27:46.720
"'Halluleja! Halluleja!'

01:27:46.810 --> 01:27:50.600
Brightly and happily the passengers'
voices resounded together.

01:27:50.680 --> 01:27:54.940
From far off in the distant,
cold depths of the sky

01:27:55.020 --> 01:27:58.020
came the clear, bracing,
indescribable blast of a trumpet."

01:27:59.030 --> 01:28:01.990
Kanta, can you hear it?
Can you hear it?

01:28:02.070 --> 01:28:05.120
Just a little further.
Just ten more meters!

01:28:05.200 --> 01:28:08.490
There's the border!
It's Japan!

01:28:09.540 --> 01:28:13.000
"I'll no longer be afraid
of that vast darkness.

01:28:13.460 --> 01:28:17.710
I'd go looking in there for what
would make people happy.

01:28:18.380 --> 01:28:21.550
You and me, always together!
Always together!

01:28:21.630 --> 01:28:23.720
Always together!
Always together!

01:28:24.430 --> 01:28:26.970
Always together,
forward we go!"

01:28:31.100 --> 01:28:33.730
"Together!

01:28:34.180 --> 01:28:38.900
Hey! Don't those fields
look so lovely?

01:28:39.730 --> 01:28:45.990
And everybody's gathered there!
That must be the real Heaven!

01:28:46.070 --> 01:28:50.620
Look! She's there!
There's my mother!"

01:28:56.960 --> 01:28:59.050
Kanta, we're home!

01:29:00.290 --> 01:29:02.460
We've come home to Japan!

01:29:06.760 --> 01:29:08.390
Kanta...

01:29:31.290 --> 01:29:36.250
<i>More than fifty years have</i>
<i>passed since all that happened.</i>

01:29:37.290 --> 01:29:42.800
<i>The island where my family lived...</i>
<i>The island where I met Tanya...</i>

01:29:43.710 --> 01:29:49.470
<i>Our island stood before us,</i>
<i>looking exactly the same.</i>

01:29:49.930 --> 01:29:53.930
<i>"Seno Family Grave"</i>

01:29:56.350 --> 01:29:59.940
We've finally managed
to come back.

01:30:01.730 --> 01:30:03.730
Kanta.

01:30:04.320 --> 01:30:06.030
Tatsuo.

01:30:12.700 --> 01:30:17.750
<i>That day, a primary school</i>
<i>graduation ceremony was held.</i>

01:30:19.750 --> 01:30:24.510
<i>For those of us who weren't</i>
<i>able to graduate back then.</i>

01:30:24.630 --> 01:30:26.670
<i>"Welcome, Visitation Group!"</i>

01:30:27.090 --> 01:30:34.560
I hereby certify you have completed
your primary school education

01:30:34.640 --> 01:30:43.150
at Shikotan National People's School
after a 56 year course of study.

01:30:49.120 --> 01:30:53.120
- Congratulations.
- Thank you, ma'am.

01:31:00.540 --> 01:31:04.590
- I'll never forget that.
- Me, neither.

01:31:04.710 --> 01:31:08.050
Wait, did that happen?

01:31:15.470 --> 01:31:17.270
Tanya!

01:31:19.270 --> 01:31:20.640
<Giovanni?>

01:31:38.200 --> 01:31:39.250
Is Tanya here?

01:31:39.370 --> 01:31:42.540
This is Nina.
She is Tanya's granddaughter.

01:31:42.620 --> 01:31:47.090
Tanya was my mother.
She passed away last year.

01:31:47.750 --> 01:31:50.380
She always said that she
hoped to see you again.

01:31:51.050 --> 01:31:53.050
So, she's gone...

01:32:16.700 --> 01:32:18.660
<i>"Night on the Galactic Railroad"</i>

01:32:19.830 --> 01:32:21.750
<What's it about?>

01:32:25.080 --> 01:32:30.090
When people die, they rise up
into the heavens

01:32:30.170 --> 01:32:32.630
and become stars
in the night sky.

01:32:33.180 --> 01:32:40.430
Those countless stars fill the sky,
shining brightly and eternally,

01:32:40.890 --> 01:32:47.980
and we live our lives down here,
basking in their light.

01:32:48.650 --> 01:32:51.070
That's what the story is about.

01:32:55.740 --> 01:32:57.580
<That's very beautiful.>

01:32:57.580 --> 01:33:02.450
<i>♪ <Along a long road, ♪</i>
<i>♪ and on a moonlit night,> ♪</i>

01:33:02.540 --> 01:33:06.500
<i>♪ <and with that song that ♪</i>
<i>♪ flies away with a jingle,> ♪</i>

01:33:06.580 --> 01:33:10.460
<i>♪ <and with that ancient, ♪</i>
<i>♪ seven-stringed guitar> ♪</i>

01:33:10.590 --> 01:33:14.010
<i>♪ <that tormented me ♪</i>
<i>♪ so much at night...> ♪</i>

01:33:30.150 --> 01:33:34.150
<Giovanni? Shall we dance, too?>
